@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@token = REPLACE_ONLY_IN_A_LOCAL_UNTRACKED_COPY

### Copy this file to requests.local.http, then set your LOCAL token there.
### Start with a fresh process. IDs are assigned by the server; adapt URLs if necessary.

### List users: 200 and [] initially
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create: 201, Location header and a server-assigned id
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Primjer Korisnika","email":"primjer@example.com"}

### Read by the id returned by POST: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update existing user: 204
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Promijenjeno Ime","email":"primjer@example.com"}

### Invalid input: 400, errors for name and email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":" ","email":"nije-email"}

### Duplicate email, case-insensitive policy: 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Druga Osoba","email":"PRIMJER@example.com"}

### Delete: 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Missing user after deletion: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Missing token: 401, independent of whether the id exists
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### Malformed JSON: 400, not 500
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":
